;; Companion to kotoba-native kernel-object-entries `aiueos-browser-key`
;; (guest browser desktop input method, ADR-0225).
;;
;; THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE THE ORACLE'S. Every key-sequence vector below was
;; produced by feeding its `:keys` to src/aiueos/compositor/ime.cljk
;; (`boot`, then `handle-key` per key) and reading back `:committed` (or
;; `:guest-log` with the IME off), `:buf`, `:preedit`, `:converting?`,
;; `:cand-idx` and `:reading`. Each step's :expected is how many code points
;; that key committed. The last step asserts the focused body (window 2,
;; seeded with 日本), the romaji length and bytes, and the conversion words.
;; The refusal vectors (-1 -2 -3 -5 -8, release) are this object's own
;; bounds, which the oracle does not have.
;;
;; Keys are Linux evdev codes: letters US layout, 57 Space, 28 Enter,
;; 14 Backspace, 1 Escape, 2 is "1" (ignored).
;; 41 is the Hankaku/Zenkaku toggle (ADR-0228); its vectors' oracle is
;; src/aiueos/compositor/desktop.cljk `set-ime` with the flipped state (the
;; hosted handle-key has no toggle key), and they also assert word 432.
;; The six vectors marked ADR-0232 do NOT take the hosted IME as oracle: with
;; nothing composed it consumes Backspace and does nothing, where
;; browser.input maps Backspace to :text/edit :delete-backward. Their bodies
;; are browser.text-edit delete-backward with the caret at the end of the body
;; (where insert-text leaves it): the last code point goes, an empty body
;; stays empty. A conversion, a romaji byte or a preedit code point is still
;; taken first, as the hosted IME takes it.
{:format :aiueos.browser-ime/v1
 :entry aiueos-browser-key
 :graph {:root aiueos.browser-ime
         :modules [aiueos.browser-ime]}
 :native {:target :x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1
          :export "kotoba_aiueos_browser_key"
          :imports []
          :required-operations [kernel-load-u32 kernel-store-u32 kernel-subregion]}
 :arguments [:surface :surface-bytes :key-code :value]
 :oracle "src/aiueos/compositor/ime.cljk handle-key"
 :result {:kind :committed-count-or-reason :range [-8 -1]}
 :reasons {-1 :null-region-or-surface-not-8192
           -2 :abi-or-window-count-outside-1-4
           -3 :focus-is-not-a-window-1-4
           -5 :the-body-would-pass-64
           -8 :romaji-buffer-full-or-preedit-overflow}
 :verification {:node-stack-size 8000
                :fuel 1048576
                :memory {:base 4096 :image-bytes 8192}
                :floors {:minimum-vectors 40
                         :minimum-steps 139
                         :minimum-memory-assertions 112}}
 :vectors
